              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
            may be thought of (see
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+and+dg-Lie+algebras"} here
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strong+homotopy+Lie+algebras"} strong homotopy Lie algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on dg-Lie algebras is one way to present this homotopy theory. This is used for instance in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+moduli+problems"} formal moduli problems
          %p
            For dg-Lie algebras in positive degree and over the rational numbers this model structure, due to (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen69"}> Quillen 69, theorem II
            ) is one of the algebraic models for presenting
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
            (see there) of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected+topological+spaces"} simply connected topological spaces
          %h2#definition Definition
          #ProjectiveModelStructureOndgLieAlgebras.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              There exists a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
              structure
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLie
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgLie_k)_{proj}
              on the category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLie
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgLie_k
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
              over a commutative
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ⊃
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \supset \mathbb{Q}
              such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+maps"} surjective maps
              %li
                %p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
                  on the underlying
                  = succeed "." do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
          %p
            For dg-Lie algebras in degrees
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ≥
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n \geq 1
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Quillen69"} Quillen 69
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Hinich97"} Hinich 97
          %p
            This becomes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+category"} simplicial category
            with simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+spaces"} mapping spaces
            given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dgLie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo ↦
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi dgLie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi 𝔥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  dgLie(\mathfrak{g}, \mathfrak{h})
                  \\coloneqq
                  ([k] \mapsto Hom_{dgLie}(\mathfrak{g} , \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^k) \otimes\mathfrak{h}))
                  \\,,
          %p where
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^k)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polynomial+differential+forms"} polynomial differential forms
                on the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi 𝔥
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^\bullet(\Delta^k)\otimes \mathfrak{h}
                is the canonical dg-Lie algebra structure on the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich97"}> Hinich 97, 4.8.2
            , following
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+dg-algebras#HomComplexes"} Bousfield &amp; Gugenheim 1976
          %p
            This enrichment satisfies together with the model structure some of the properties of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+model+category"} simplicial model category
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich97"}> Hinich 97, 4.8.3, 4.8.4
            ), but not all of them.
          %h2#Properties Properties
          %h3#RectificationResolution
            Relation to
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            dg-Lie algebras with this model structure are a
            %em rectification
            of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Lie
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lie
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+operad"} Lie operad
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Lie
            its standard
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrant+resolution"} cofibrant resolution
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebras+over+an+operad"} algebras over an operad
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Lie
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Lie
            in chain complexes are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-Lie+algebras"} dg-Lie algebras
            and algebras over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo ^
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat Lie
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} L-∞ algebras
            and by the rectification result discussed at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras+over+an+operad"} model structure on dg-algebras over an operad
            there is an induced
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mover
                    %mi Lie
                    %mo ^
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mo ≃
                  %mi Alg
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Lie
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Alg(\widehat Lie) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} Alg(Lie)
          %p
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
            which is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transferred+model+structure"} transferred
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+chain+complexes"} model structure on chain complexes
            (unbounded propjective) to the above model structure on chain complexes.
          %p
            There is also a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            from the model structure on dg-Lie algebras to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+stack"} derived
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stacks"} ∞-stacks
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+moduli+problems"}> formal moduli problems
            ”). More on this is at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
          %p
            Specifically, there is (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen"}> Quillen 69
            ) an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℛ
                  %mo ⊣
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi dgLie
                  %mover
                    %munder
                      %mo →
                      %mi i
                    %mover
                      %mo ←
                      %mi ℛ
                  %mi dgCoCAlg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\mathcal{R} \dashv i) \;\colon\;
                  dgLie \stackrel{\overset{\mathcal{R}}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{i}{\to}} dgCoCAlg
          %p
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
            and dg-Lie algebras, where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            is the (non-full) inclusion that regards a dg-Lie algebra as a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded+coalgebra"} differential graded coalgebra
            with co-binary differential, and where the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℛ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{R}
            (“rectification”) sends a dg-coalgebra to a dg-Lie algebra whose underlying graded
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+Lie+algebra"} free Lie algebra
            on the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
            0, this adjunction is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dgCoCAlg
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgCoCAlg
            and the model structure on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dgLie
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgLie
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, theorem 3.2
            ).
          %p
            In particular, therefore the composite
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi ℛ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \circ \mathcal{R}
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            functor for
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
          %p
            For more see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+and+dg-Lie+algebras"} relation between L-∞ algebras and dg-Lie algebras
          %h3#RelationToDgCoalgebras Relation to dg-coalgebras
          %p
            Via the above relation to
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebras"} dg-coalgebras
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            be of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
          #CEfunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Chevalley-Eilenberg dg-coalgebra)
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLieAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi dgCocAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE
                    \\;\colon\;
                    dgLieAlg_{k}
                    \\longrightarrow
                    dgCocAlg_k
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              functor. It sends a dg-Lie algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathfrak{g}, \partial, [-,-])
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-coalgebra"} dg-coalgebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ∂
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %msup
                        %mo ∨
                        %mo •
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    CE(\mathfrak{g},\partial,[-,-])
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\left(
                    \\vee^\bullet \mathfrak{g}[1]
                    ,\;
                    D = \partial + [-,-]
                    \\right)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right the extension of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ∂
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [-,-]
              to graded
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivations"} derivations
              is understood.
          %p
            For dg-Lie algebras concentrated in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n \geq 1
            this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen"}> Quillen 69, appendix B, prop 6.2
            ). For unbounded dg-algebras, this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, 2.2.2
            ).
          #LeftAdjointToCEfunctor.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi dgCocalg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,D) \in dgCocalg_k
              write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≔
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mover
                        %mi X
                        %mo ¯
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %mo ∂
                      %mo ≔
                      %mi D
                      %mo +
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi Δ
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi id
                      %mo −
                      %mi id
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLieAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{L}(X,D)
                    \\coloneqq
                    \\left(
                    F(\overline{X}[-1]),\;
                    \\partial \coloneqq D + (\Delta - 1 \otimes id - id \otimes 1)
                    \\right)
                    \\;\in dgLieAlg_k\;
            %p where
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi ker
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi ϵ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{X} \coloneqq ker(\epsilon)
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kernel"} kernel
                  of the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counit"} counit
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  is the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+Lie+algebra"} free Lie algebra
                  functor (as graded Lie algebras);
              %li
                %p
                  on the right we are extending
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi Δ
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mi id
                        %mo −
                        %mi id
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo ⊗
                        %mover
                          %mi X
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Delta - 1 \otimes id - id \otimes 1) \colon \overline{X} \to \overline{X} \otimes \overline{X}
                  as a Lie algebra
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
          %p
            For dg-Lie algebras concentrated in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n \geq 1
            this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen"}> Quillen 69, appendix B, prop 6.1
            ). For unbounded dg-algebras, this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, 2.2.1
            ).
          #CEAdjunction.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              from def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEfunctor"}
              and def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LeftAdjointToCEfunctor"}
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint
              to each other:
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLieAlg
                      %mi k
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi CE
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi ℒ
                    %msub
                      %mi dgCocAlg
                      %mi k
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    dgLieAlg_k
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{CE}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\mathcal{L}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    dgCocAlg_k
                    \\,.
            %p
              Moreover, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi dgCocAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in dgCocAlg_k
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLieAlg
                      %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g} \in dgLieAlg_k
              then the adjoint
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom+sets"} hom sets
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi MC
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo ¯
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(\mathcal{L}(X), \mathfrak{g})
                    \\simeq
                    Hom(X, CE(\mathfrak{g}))
                    \\simeq
                    MC(Hom(\overline{X},\mathfrak{g}))
            %p
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+elements"} Maurer-Cartan elements
              in the Hom-dgLie algebra from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mover
                      %mi X
                      %mo ¯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \overline{X}
              to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
          %p
            For dg-Lie algebras concentrated in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n \geq 1
            this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen"}> Quillen 69, appendix B, somewhere
            ). For unbounded dg-algebras, this is due to (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, 2.2.5
            ).
          #QuillenAdjunctionCE.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              The adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L} \dashv CE)
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CEAdjunction"}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
              between then projective
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-Lie+algebras"} model structure on dg-Lie algebras
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLieAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi CE
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgCocAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (dgLieAlg_k)_{proj}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{CE}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\mathcal{L}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    (dgCocAlg_k)_{Quillen}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, lemma 5.2.2, lemma 5.2.3
            )
          %p Moreover:
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_4 Proposition
            %p
              In non-negatively graded dg-coalgebras, both
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+functors"} Quillen functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℒ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{L} \dashv CE)
              from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunctionCE"}
              preserve all
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphisms"} quasi-isomorphisms
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+unit"} adjunction unit
              and the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction+counit"} adjunction counit
              are quasi-isomorphisms.
          %p
            For dg-algebras in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n \geq 1
            this is (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen76"}> Quillen 76, theorem 7.5
            ). In unbounded degrees this is (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, prop. 3.3.2
            )
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The Quillen adjunctin from prop.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#QuillenAdjunctionCE"}
              is a
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgLieAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mrow
                          %mphantom
                            %mi qu
                        %msub
                          %mo ≃
                          %mi Qu
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi CE
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi ℒ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgCocAlg
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Quillen
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (dgLieAlg_k)_{proj}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{CE}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\mathcal{L}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {{}_{\phantom{qu}}\simeq_{Qu}}
                    (dgCocAlg_k)_{Quillen}
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Hinich98"}> Hinich 98, theorem 3.2
            ) using (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen76"}> Quillen 76 II 1.4
            )
          %h3#relation_to_simplicial_lie_algebras Relation to simplicial Lie algebras
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normalized+chains+complex"} normalized chains complex
            functor from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+Lie+algebras"} simplicial Lie algebras
            constitutes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            from the projective
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+Lie+algebras"} model structure on simplicial Lie algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "model+structure+on+simplicial+Lie+algebras#QuillenAdjunctionTodgLieAlgebras"} there
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+Lie+algebras"} model structure on simplicial Lie algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+for+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras"} model structure for L-∞ algebras
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relation+between+L-%E2%88%9E+algebras+and+dg-Lie+algebras"} relation between L-∞ algebras and dg-Lie algebras
          %h2#references References
          %p
            The model structure on dg-Lie algebras in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            and in degrees
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≥
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \geq n \geq 1
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Quillen69
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dan+Quillen"}> Dan Quillen
              , section II.5 and appendix B of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Rational homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.jstor.org/stable/1970725"} JSTOR
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.math.northwestern.edu/~konter/gtrs/rational.pdf"} pdf
          %p This is extended to a model structure on dg-Lie algebras in unbounded degrees in
          %ul
            %li#Hinich97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homological algebra of homotopy algebras
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/q-alg/9702015"} arXiv:q-alg/9702015
              %em Erratum
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0309453"}> arXiv:math/0309453
              ))
          %p
            and the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-coalgebras"} model structure on dg-coalgebras
            in unbounded degrees is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Hinich98
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vladimir+Hinich"}> Vladimir Hinich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em DG coalgebras as formal stacks
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/9812034"} arXiv:math/9812034
          %p See also section 2.1 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Formal+moduli+problems"} Formal moduli problems
          %p
            Review with discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+limits"} homotopy limits
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimits"} homotopy colimits
            is in
          %ul
            %li#Walter06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ben+Walter"}> Ben Walter
              , section 4 of
              %em Rational Homotopy Calculus of Functors
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0603336"}> arXiv:math/0603336
              )
        .revisedby
